WEBVTT

00:03.740 --> 00:09.790
We lost countless precious lives
 in that last Void attack.

00:10.490 --> 00:14.580
And our Last Town has suffered gravely.

00:15.600 --> 00:22.500
QJ of the Nine Soldiers gave his life to protect 
the light of the Soul Future from the Voids.

00:22.870 --> 00:25.240
We cannot lose that light.

00:26.750 --> 00:31.000
Now is the time for us all 
to band together as one,

00:31.000 --> 00:34.860
and stop the Ultimate Void 
from ever emerging.

02:07.020 --> 02:12.520
Episode 10: CHAOS

02:08.680 --> 02:13.380
Apparently, it looked just like something 
Natsuko had summoned before with her magic.

02:13.380 --> 02:15.310
That Void from the other day, you mean?

02:15.560 --> 02:19.020
Didn't she say she came 
from the Kingdom of Reality?

02:19.020 --> 02:21.310
I've never even heard of the place.

02:21.310 --> 02:24.460
Then, where the hell did 
this Natsuko come from?

02:25.430 --> 02:28.450
This area has been pretty much evacuated.

02:28.780 --> 02:33.330
Our biggest problem is that it'll take 
some time to repair the ramparts.

02:33.330 --> 02:35.080
We'll have men take turns keeping watch,

02:35.080 --> 02:38.890
but currently, we could honestly 
be attacked by Voids anywhere.

02:39.350 --> 02:40.590
How's Natsuko?

02:40.850 --> 02:43.730
She's still not in any state to draw.

02:44.070 --> 02:47.480
The Voids are starting to copy 
the things Natsuko drew.

02:50.200 --> 02:55.210
If the things she drew are 
now helping the Voids attack,

02:55.210 --> 02:57.050
it's obvious she can't draw right now.

02:57.710 --> 02:59.990
We'll remove Natsuko from the team for now.

03:01.310 --> 03:06.000
And if the same Void shows up again,
how are we supposed to fight it?

03:08.240 --> 03:09.990
Without QJ,

03:10.330 --> 03:14.250
we have no way of knowing 
when the Voids will appear.

03:22.530 --> 03:23.890
Back then...

03:24.250 --> 03:27.930
If only I hadn't told QJ 
how <i>A Tale of Perishing</i> ends.

03:28.650 --> 03:30.230
Back then...

03:30.230 --> 03:32.230
If only I'd been able to draw something.

03:32.930 --> 03:34.230
If only I'd...

03:38.540 --> 03:39.550
I'm coming in.

03:40.860 --> 03:44.520
We're low on food, 
so this was about all I could make.

03:45.340 --> 03:48.460
QJ grew these vegetables.

03:50.690 --> 03:52.120
So make sure you eat it.

03:54.080 --> 03:55.380
Natsuko.

03:55.380 --> 03:58.230
Make sure we get a happy ending.

03:58.230 --> 04:01.510
I know you'll be able to change the future.

04:02.720 --> 04:03.840
Luke.

04:09.430 --> 04:10.660
Thanks for the food.

04:17.820 --> 04:19.060
QJ...

04:20.240 --> 04:23.330
What am I supposed to do?

04:40.320 --> 04:43.130
I brought medicinal herbs 
and food from our garden.

04:43.130 --> 04:44.930
You're a lifesaver!

04:46.230 --> 04:50.510
I've been getting more 
and more people by the day.

04:52.930 --> 04:54.420
Great Hero.

04:54.970 --> 04:58.300
Voids destroyed my fields.

04:58.300 --> 05:01.230
We lost everything.

05:01.230 --> 05:06.480
If I'm going to be a burden, 
could you let me just die here?

05:06.480 --> 05:08.120
What are you talking about?

05:08.120 --> 05:11.140
As long as the Soul Future's shining,
 everything will be okay.

05:11.760 --> 05:13.630
Peace will come again.

05:14.000 --> 05:17.080
I'll protect everyone, so don't worry.

05:26.090 --> 05:28.250
Unio, go on and head back first.

05:28.250 --> 05:29.060
Huh?

05:30.990 --> 05:32.000
What's wrong?

05:32.000 --> 05:33.010
Oh.

05:33.010 --> 05:37.150
Um, my husband hasn't come home yet.

05:37.150 --> 05:39.370
Don't worry. Let's look for him together.

05:39.370 --> 05:40.530
Luke.

05:42.260 --> 05:46.030
You haven't eaten since this morning,
 right? And you haven't slept.

05:46.030 --> 05:47.930
You need to rest a little.

05:47.930 --> 05:49.960
Oh, Great Hero.

05:49.960 --> 05:51.190
Great Hero.

05:52.720 --> 05:53.630
Unio.

05:54.300 --> 05:56.580
Everyone's really anxious.

06:13.130 --> 06:15.800
Didn't expect to see you here.

06:18.310 --> 06:22.550
Luke keeps prioritizing 
the people of the town.

06:22.550 --> 06:25.320
He's been giving them his food,

06:25.320 --> 06:28.170
and lately, he hasn't slept at all.

06:29.350 --> 06:30.820
Is everything all right?

06:31.240 --> 06:33.120
Honestly, this might be really bad.

06:34.320 --> 06:36.940
He's blaming himself really hard.

06:38.410 --> 06:40.810
Just like when our friends died.

06:41.650 --> 06:44.560
Actually, this might be worse.

06:45.010 --> 06:48.300
At this rate, I think Luke may lose it.

06:48.300 --> 06:50.260
I'm talking about <i>you</i>, Unio.

06:50.260 --> 06:50.960
What?

06:51.580 --> 06:54.010
Are <i>you</i> all right?

06:54.400 --> 06:57.730
No one's okay when they lose a friend.

07:01.450 --> 07:03.120
Do you remember...

07:03.120 --> 07:08.800
that one time QJ caught a giant fish for us
 because we were starving?

07:10.560 --> 07:12.740
How could I ever forget?

07:13.020 --> 07:18.880
That fish ended up being a relative of 
Admiral's, and we never heard the end of it.

07:22.280 --> 07:27.030
QJ was a piece of scrap, but a real great guy.

07:27.390 --> 07:30.290
He really loved gardening.

07:30.610 --> 07:35.000
He's probably watering some flowers
with Chingosman right now.

07:35.850 --> 07:37.140
Up in heaven.

07:38.410 --> 07:39.620
Yeah.

07:42.150 --> 07:46.770
He basically died in my place.

07:47.190 --> 07:51.380
If only my self-destruct 
spell had succeeded.

07:54.170 --> 07:55.390
QJ...

07:56.150 --> 07:59.020
You dumb piece of scrap.

07:59.610 --> 08:03.670
How dare you...

08:04.370 --> 08:06.300
be cooler than me...

08:07.140 --> 08:08.430
in the end?

08:14.140 --> 08:18.290
QJ!

08:26.210 --> 08:30.190
Justice, can you do something about Luke?

08:30.690 --> 08:33.170
I'm not the one who can help him.

08:33.530 --> 08:38.840
But Luke was talking to you about something,
 wasn't he? I just can't help him with this.

08:38.840 --> 08:40.380
You're right. You can't.

08:41.700 --> 08:45.950
There's only one person 
who can help Luke right now.

08:48.690 --> 08:49.780
Memmeln?

08:49.780 --> 08:50.960
It's Natsuko.

08:53.460 --> 08:56.930
Luke's changed a lot 
since Natsuko showed up.

08:57.390 --> 09:01.220
You've been by Luke's side 
ever since you two were born, right?

09:01.220 --> 09:04.970
Luke's been burdened by the 
weighty title of "hero" all this time.

09:05.230 --> 09:09.470
Have you ever seen him 
have so much fun before?

09:11.730 --> 09:12.650
Sure I have.

09:12.980 --> 09:17.380
I see your habit of sticking your tail 
straight up when you're lying hasn't changed.

09:17.980 --> 09:19.660
Sh-Shut up.

09:20.690 --> 09:24.200
We're not the ones 
who can help Luke out this time.

09:24.660 --> 09:25.690
It's Natsuko.

09:26.330 --> 09:28.420
You know that, don't you?

09:38.920 --> 09:43.590
This is just a rumor I heard, 
but did you hear <i>how</i> Master QJ died?

09:43.590 --> 09:44.550
What?

09:44.550 --> 09:45.730
'Cause of Natsuko.

09:45.730 --> 09:47.030
No way.

09:47.030 --> 09:51.280
People are saying the Great Hero
 might be her next victim.

09:51.280 --> 09:54.870
More Voids <i>have</i> been showing up 
ever since that woman appeared.

09:54.870 --> 09:58.150
I hear that when Natsuko draws a picture,
it turns into a Void and appears.

09:58.150 --> 10:00.130
What's this flyer?

10:00.130 --> 10:02.150
What the heck is "Voidism"?

10:02.150 --> 10:06.280
What? Natsuko can summon the Ultimate Void?

10:06.280 --> 10:09.740
Natsuko was <i>trying</i> to 
summon the Ultimate Void?

10:09.740 --> 10:12.000
Natsuko's betrayed us!

10:12.000 --> 10:17.500
Haven't we faced so many hardships
 since Natsuko arrived?

10:17.500 --> 10:22.220
It's all Natsuko's fault. 
She's trying to destroy our world.

10:22.220 --> 10:27.600
Natsuko's summoning Voids with her magic 
so that she can summon the Ultimate Void.

10:27.600 --> 10:28.680
Traitor.

10:28.680 --> 10:29.940
Traitor!

10:29.940 --> 10:31.170
Traitor.

10:31.170 --> 10:33.070
Natsuko's a traitor.

10:33.070 --> 10:34.430
Traitor.

10:34.430 --> 10:37.420
Natsuko's a traitor!

10:45.920 --> 10:49.500
I see. So that's what happens to Luke.

10:49.840 --> 10:54.220
That's what happens in the version
 of <i>A Tale of Perishing</i> I saw.

10:54.940 --> 10:55.990
Luke turns into...

10:56.440 --> 10:58.600
...the Ultimate Void.

10:59.510 --> 11:01.400
I see.

11:01.400 --> 11:06.240
I thought everything would be okay 
because it's been so peaceful all this time.

11:06.750 --> 11:08.910
I thought about telling Luke,

11:09.470 --> 11:11.650
but I don't think he'd believe me.

11:12.110 --> 11:14.020
And even if he did believe me,

11:14.020 --> 11:18.350
I'm scared Luke would
 just blame himself, and...

11:18.950 --> 11:20.890
maybe even end up killing himself.

11:21.620 --> 11:22.570
What should I—

11:22.570 --> 11:23.720
It's no use.

11:24.530 --> 11:25.320
What?

11:25.750 --> 11:28.410
It's no use, no matter what we do.

11:30.100 --> 11:33.710
B-But you said the ancient texts
 spoke of the Nine Soldiers

11:33.710 --> 11:36.750
as "the ones who can stop the 
Ultimate Void and save the world."

11:36.750 --> 11:40.360
You said the Nine Soldiers would 
"become the true light to shine upon us all."

11:40.970 --> 11:44.930
Yes, and the Nine Soldiers truly are our hope.

11:44.930 --> 11:45.770
Huh?

11:46.110 --> 11:51.270
Rather than spending our days cowering in 
anxiety and fear until we meet our demise,

11:51.780 --> 11:57.280
don't you think it's better 
to have even just a sliver of hope?

11:58.270 --> 12:02.100
That's what the Nine Soldiers are to us.

12:02.100 --> 12:05.670
They are, without a doubt, our light.

12:05.670 --> 12:07.150
But...

12:07.440 --> 12:10.700
So Luke turns into the Ultimate Void?

12:10.700 --> 12:12.090
I see.

12:12.500 --> 12:16.330
That may just be our destiny.

12:17.140 --> 12:20.420
Eventually, this world will end.

12:21.210 --> 12:24.930
It's no use, no matter what we do.

12:31.320 --> 12:32.620
Destiny!

12:34.050 --> 12:36.100
You seen that bird around here lately?

12:36.100 --> 12:39.110
That weird bird that's a cross
 between a crane and a turtle.

12:39.110 --> 12:40.590
No, I haven't.

12:40.590 --> 12:43.540
I wonder where it went. 
I have a ton of questions I want to ask it.

12:44.140 --> 12:45.980
Uh, Destiny?

12:46.590 --> 12:49.310
Why are you dressed like that?

12:49.820 --> 12:51.490
Destiny!

12:51.490 --> 12:52.840
The Chairman?

12:52.840 --> 12:55.050
My wife, Destiny.

12:55.050 --> 12:58.500
No matter how poor this world becomes,
 my wealth will never die.

12:59.370 --> 13:04.360
When you become my wife, 
I'll grant your every wish.

13:05.180 --> 13:06.540
Ciao.

13:07.530 --> 13:09.100
What's going on?

13:09.100 --> 13:11.130
I'm engaged to the Chairman.

13:11.130 --> 13:11.860
What?

13:12.250 --> 13:14.620
The Chairman is a really wonderful person.

13:14.620 --> 13:19.230
A lot of children lost their homes
 after that air raid.

13:19.230 --> 13:23.890
But the Chairman said 
he would save the Serval Cat House.

13:24.830 --> 13:28.300
I can't protect all of these kids on my own.

13:37.400 --> 13:41.290
Is it really no use, no matter what we do?

13:47.330 --> 13:52.000
<i>Unio's funeral ended up happening,
 but it was for QJ instead.</i>

13:52.900 --> 13:55.160
<i>Destiny is engaged to the Chairman.</i>

13:56.380 --> 13:59.270
<i>Everything's being forced back 
to the movie's original story.</i>

13:59.520 --> 14:01.490
<i>Which means the next plot point is...</i>

14:02.360 --> 14:05.780
<i>Memmeln tries to summon the Ultimate Void,</i>

14:06.240 --> 14:08.350
<i>and Luke kills Memmeln.</i>

14:08.790 --> 14:10.510
<i>What am I going to do?</i>

14:11.530 --> 14:12.790
It's Natsuko.

14:22.580 --> 14:23.670
Huh.

14:29.550 --> 14:32.800
Halt. This place is currently off limits.

14:36.870 --> 14:39.450
Oh, Lady Memmeln?

14:44.480 --> 14:45.880
Good work.

14:49.830 --> 14:52.400
This still isn't enough.

14:52.400 --> 14:54.330
This is one of the Nine Soldiers.

14:54.330 --> 14:57.110
There's no more time. We have to do it now.

14:57.110 --> 14:58.390
What are you doing?

14:59.120 --> 15:00.330
Great Hero.

15:00.330 --> 15:03.040
This place has been closed off.
 Head to the shelter.

15:03.040 --> 15:04.110
Ow.

15:05.080 --> 15:10.350
"Lady Natsuko is going to 
summon the Ultimate Void."

15:10.350 --> 15:14.340
"She's the savior who arrived 
from the Kingdom of Reality."

15:14.340 --> 15:16.470
"Worship Lady Natsuko"?

15:16.880 --> 15:19.580
That's the flyer those Voidism rats
 have been handing out.

15:19.580 --> 15:22.630
Natsuko is a Voidism priest!

15:22.630 --> 15:23.950
Voidism?

15:23.950 --> 15:26.160
What are you guys talking about?

15:26.160 --> 15:27.980
Great Hero. Master Unio.

15:27.980 --> 15:30.110
Please fight with us.

15:30.110 --> 15:33.370
We're going to fight for our town.

15:33.370 --> 15:34.320
Great Hero!

15:34.320 --> 15:35.150
Great Hero.

15:35.150 --> 15:36.000
Great Hero!

15:36.000 --> 15:37.180
You must decide!

15:36.300 --> 15:37.610
Great Hero!

15:37.180 --> 15:40.790
The hunt for the traitor, 
Natsuko, has already begun!

15:41.840 --> 15:42.840
Don't tell me...

15:42.840 --> 15:44.660
Please wait, Great Hero!

15:44.000 --> 15:45.640
Natsuko's deceiving you!

15:45.640 --> 15:47.440
We're out of time!

15:47.440 --> 15:48.800
She's a traitor!

15:52.360 --> 15:55.090
What's going on with everyone?

15:56.590 --> 15:57.610
Stop this!

15:57.610 --> 15:59.400
There! A Void!

15:59.840 --> 16:01.600
It's the Ultimate Void!

16:01.600 --> 16:02.960
That's a drawing Natsuko drew!

16:02.960 --> 16:04.090
But that's...

16:05.720 --> 16:06.530
No!

16:06.530 --> 16:09.720
She's trying to summon the Ultimate Void!

16:09.720 --> 16:10.520
You're wrong.

16:10.520 --> 16:11.490
That's proof!

16:12.640 --> 16:15.490
We have our proof!

16:17.120 --> 16:18.910
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

16:18.910 --> 16:21.120
Calm down! Calm down, everyone!

16:22.890 --> 16:23.760
Unio.

16:24.600 --> 16:27.860
Natsuko's somewhere in town.
 She isn't here.

16:27.860 --> 16:29.960
We need to split up and 
find her before they do.

16:29.960 --> 16:30.980
Got it.

16:44.010 --> 16:50.820
Lady Natsuko is the one who will summon 
the Ultimate Void and end this world for us.

16:50.820 --> 16:56.030
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

16:51.350 --> 16:56.030
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

16:58.160 --> 17:01.610
Lady Natsuko will save us all.

17:01.610 --> 17:02.240
Huh?

17:02.240 --> 17:03.610
Lady Natsuko!

17:03.910 --> 17:04.980
Lady Natsuko!

17:04.980 --> 17:08.480
Please summon the 
Ultimate Void immediately.

17:06.700 --> 17:09.910
Huh? Wh-Wh-What are you talking about?

17:10.380 --> 17:11.680
<i>Voidism believers?</i>

17:11.680 --> 17:14.150
<i>Huh? Wait, but Memmeln...</i>

17:14.150 --> 17:15.180
There's Natsuko!

17:15.180 --> 17:16.950
We found Natsuko!

17:16.950 --> 17:18.680
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

17:18.680 --> 17:19.750
H-Huh?

17:19.750 --> 17:21.260
Lady Natsuko is our light!

17:21.260 --> 17:22.760
Don't let Natsuko get away with—

17:24.360 --> 17:25.950
Hey, stop that!

17:25.950 --> 17:27.690
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

17:26.930 --> 17:28.570
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

17:27.690 --> 17:29.230
Lady Natsuko is our light!

17:29.230 --> 17:32.250
No, really, I'm not! 
You've all got the wrong idea!

17:32.250 --> 17:34.310
Don't let Natsuko get away with this!

17:41.250 --> 17:44.630
<i>The story of </i>A Tale of Perishing<i>'s 
not just back to how it was.</i>

17:44.630 --> 17:48.560
<i>It's now somehow even worse
 because I showed up.</i>

17:48.560 --> 17:49.840
A Void!

17:54.970 --> 17:57.460
Lady Natsuko has summoned a Void for us!

17:56.490 --> 17:59.000
Natsuko summoned another Void!

17:58.530 --> 17:59.730
<i>But that's...</i>

18:12.520 --> 18:13.870
Everyone, run!

18:17.710 --> 18:19.640
Natsuko's the source of all the Voids.

18:19.640 --> 18:22.250
Maybe if we kill Natsuko,
the Voids will die, too.

18:22.250 --> 18:24.250
Yeah! Let's kill Natsuko!

18:24.670 --> 18:26.000
Kill Natsuko!

18:28.750 --> 18:30.240
Protect Lady Natsuko!

18:35.060 --> 18:38.010
This is no time to fight! Get to shelter!

18:42.150 --> 18:45.130
<i>The things I draw...</i>

18:49.690 --> 18:51.440
Kill Natsuko!

18:52.040 --> 18:55.440
Kill Natsuko! Kill Natsuko!

18:57.460 --> 18:58.450
This way.

19:15.350 --> 19:17.390
Natsuko, go on ahead.

19:21.190 --> 19:24.830
<i>The things I draw are becoming Voids.</i>

19:26.180 --> 19:27.700
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

19:29.510 --> 19:32.670
Sally, I think this goes here.

19:33.410 --> 19:34.980
See? A perfect fit.

19:35.220 --> 19:38.520
Meg, we're not supposed 
to be having fun here.

19:38.520 --> 19:41.100
We're about to use a forbidden spell.

19:41.820 --> 19:44.690
B-But I'm not having fun.

19:59.490 --> 20:00.890
<i>I have to draw.</i>

20:01.340 --> 20:03.840
<i>I have to draw something.</i>

20:11.310 --> 20:12.520
Luke!

20:13.710 --> 20:15.160
Are you okay?

20:15.160 --> 20:16.370
<i>I...</i>

20:17.220 --> 20:19.660
<i>It's because I couldn't draw anything.</i>

20:20.000 --> 20:22.160
<i>It's because I failed.</i>

20:22.450 --> 20:26.040
<i>The things I draw are 
going to kill everyone.</i>

20:26.660 --> 20:28.410
I've found Natsuko!

20:28.410 --> 20:30.580
Kill Natsuko!

20:28.810 --> 20:30.840
Kill Natsuko!

20:38.620 --> 20:39.480
Natsuko!

20:47.060 --> 20:48.470
Great Hero?

20:58.320 --> 21:00.060
Luke, no!

21:01.200 --> 21:02.960
Mommy!

21:04.980 --> 21:05.900
No!

21:10.470 --> 21:12.270
Mommy!

21:17.540 --> 21:18.540
You dummy!

21:23.940 --> 21:25.800
It's Natsuko!

21:25.800 --> 21:26.880
It's Natsuko!

21:26.880 --> 21:28.330
Kill Natsuko!

21:34.010 --> 21:35.100
Natsuko!

21:35.100 --> 21:36.890
Unio!

21:43.440 --> 21:45.480
Kill her!

21:46.440 --> 21:48.190
Stop!

22:00.080 --> 22:01.380
It disappeared?

22:01.380 --> 22:03.460
Did we do it?

22:03.460 --> 22:05.380
I think we did.

22:05.380 --> 22:08.350
Yeah! We did it!

22:08.350 --> 22:09.900
We did it!

22:09.900 --> 22:11.840
We defeated Natsuko!

23:49.990 --> 23:54.900
<b>Episode 11: DESPAIR</b>
